            <ArticleTitle>Unstable angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1013-4, 1016-7, 1021-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In recent years, there have been considerable advances in our understanding of the complex pathophysiology of unstable angina. A number of therapeutic options are now available. This article reviews current concepts of pathophysiology and summarises clinical features, natural history and available treatments.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
